# 📘 **Phase 3 — Part 3: VPC + Networking + Security Architecture**

## ⭐ Project Overview  
This project demonstrates how to build secure, isolated, production‑grade cloud networks using AWS VPC, subnets, routing, NAT Gateway, Internet Gateway, Security Groups, NACLs, IAM roles, and multi‑tier EC2 deployment.

I performed hands‑on tasks including creating a VPC, building public and private subnets, configuring route tables, deploying NAT Gateway, launching EC2 instances in both subnets, testing connectivity, validating IAM roles, and deploying a web server.

This represents real cloud network engineering work.

---

## ⭐ What I Built  
- IAM role with correct trust + permission policies  
- Custom VPC  
- Public subnet  
- Private subnet  
- Internet Gateway  
- NAT Gateway  
- Route tables for each subnet  
- Security Groups (public + private)  
- NACLs (public + private)  
- EC2 instance in public subnet  
- EC2 instance in private subnet  
- SSH access via public EC2 → private EC2  
- Outbound internet access via NAT Gateway  
- Apache web server deployment in public subnet  

